ergy the  conservation of momentum absolutely  crucial to the way that physics  functions to a the natural world  functions but they're not sacrosanct  they're not things that once we  understand them we're not allowed to  question them anymore physics is a  breathing living thing at least if you  count physics as not how the universe  behaves but our understanding of the  universe our understanding of the  universe is never perfect it hopefully  gets better but it certainly changes  over time so things that you might have  thought we're absolutely inviolable  principles things that could not  possibly be violated once you understand  how the universe works better it might  be that those principles are just  special cases that are approximately  true in the right circumstances but not  true more generally that's a lesson for  us as physicists and maybe a lesson for  us whenever we think about the world in  any context whatsoever
 

